narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1035: trailing whitespace.
+*One by one they said their names. Brin said hers last, quietly, as if it cost more.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1041: trailing whitespace.
+**Brin:** B-R-. It used to be longer.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1042: trailing whitespace.
+**Shrine Keeper:** I can recut it. I keep a chisel for the register board.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1043: trailing whitespace.
+**Brin:** If you cut it, it will just be your letters.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1044: trailing whitespace.
+**Shrine Keeper:** Then say his name while I cut. Then the letters are yours.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1045: trailing whitespace.
+**Brin:** Bram Alder. He could split a log with one swing and could not split a word to save his life.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1046: trailing whitespace.
+*The chisel bit. The name held.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1052: trailing whitespace.
+**Brin:** If I hold the east roof, the west falls. If I hold the west—  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1053: trailing whitespace.
+**Nixie:** You said that at the shrine. Word for word. I was there.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1054: trailing whitespace.
+**Brin:** And he said I did not have to hold it alone.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1055: trailing whitespace.
+**Brin:** Everyone who can lift, to the west roof. Children to the east. Now!  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1056: trailing whitespace.
+*Twelve pairs of hands took the west beam. Brin held the east alone, and for once it was the smaller weight.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1057: trailing whitespace.
+**Nixie:** Twelve hands and one stubborn woodcutter. That is a road.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1063: trailing whitespace.
