narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1688: trailing whitespace.
+**Jori:** A key. Something that opens the lock instead of smashing the door. My family made the lock. I will make the key.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1689: trailing whitespace.
+**Mahmut:** How long?  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1690: trailing whitespace.
+**Jori:** Longer than I want. Shorter than she needs, if I stop talking. Go away.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1698: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** I read your treason aloud in eleven villages. "The knight Mahmut, oath-breaker, abandoned the heir."  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1699: trailing whitespace.
+**Mahmut:** You believed it.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1700: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** I believed it was paper. Paper is what heralds carry. I stopped carrying paper after that.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1701: trailing whitespace.
+**Mahmut:** And now?  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1702: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** Now I carry people. They are heavier and more honest.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1708: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** One for the road and two for the rain, three for the ones who will walk it again.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1709: trailing whitespace.
+**Nara:** Your rhythm is off by a half-step on the uphill.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1710: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** On purpose. The old ones need the half-step.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1711: trailing whitespace.
+**Nara:** ...That is good wardening.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1717: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** Hear me. Six years ago I read you a decree. It was false. The knight Mahmut did not abandon the heir. He defied the order to give her up.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1718: trailing whitespace.
+*The square was silent. Then an old woman said, "Then who gave the order?"*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1719: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** That, grandmother, is the right question. Ask it loudly.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1725: trailing whitespace.
+**Fadyme:** You never fly a banner.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1726: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** A banner tells people where to march. I would rather they decided.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1727: trailing whitespace.
+**Fadyme:** Then where will you march next?  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1728: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** Wherever he goes looking for that Court. Someone has to keep the rhythm.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1743: trailing whitespace.
+**Pippa:** Rule of the Harvest Supper: one dish, one name. You say the name, you get a bowl.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1744: trailing whitespace.
+**Kera:** I brought a dish. It is technically soup.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1745: trailing whitespace.
+**Jori:** It is moving.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1746: trailing whitespace.
+**Kera:** It is effervescent.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1747: trailing whitespace.
+**Nixie:** I will eat it! For the festival!  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1748: trailing whitespace.
+*Nixie ate it. Nixie was fine. Nixie glowed faintly for an hour.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1754: trailing whitespace.
+**Innkeeper:** After Crownfall, travelers stopped paying. So we stopped charging. Twice a day, a meal, no coin.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1755: trailing whitespace.
+**Fadyme:** That is generous.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1756: trailing whitespace.
+**Innkeeper:** It is practical. A fed traveler says their name at the door. A hungry one slips past the register.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1757: trailing whitespace.
+**Mahmut:** So the meal is a count.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1758: trailing whitespace.
+**Innkeeper:** The meal is a meal, knight. The count is a bonus.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1764: trailing whitespace.
+**Pippa:** Last verse! Everyone who brought a name, sing it with me!  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1765: trailing whitespace.
+*Two hundred voices, off-key and loud. Somewhere, a bell rang, and nobody stopped singing.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1766: trailing whitespace.
+**Fadyme (thought):** *The bell cannot count a square this loud. For one night, it is losing.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1776: trailing whitespace.
+**Clem:** Sun-Eclipse Day. Once a year the villages say the black sun breathes.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1777: trailing whitespace.
+**Vespera:** Does it?  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1778: trailing whitespace.
+**Clem:** Every grave-keeper's record says yes. Every scholar's says no. I trust grave-keepers.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1784: trailing whitespace.
+**Thistle:** The owing-bells are all opening. All of them. The whole ridge.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1785: trailing whitespace.
+**Vespera:** It is not breathing. It is recounting. Every owed hour in the valley, checked at once.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1786: trailing whitespace.
+**Thistle:** Why t-today?  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1787: trailing whitespace.
+**Vespera:** Because someone set a day for it. Machines keep calendars. So do chancellors.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1793: trailing whitespace.
+**Clem:** Sun-Eclipse tokens. Superstition. I am keeping five.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1794: trailing whitespace.
+**Thistle:** Why five?  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1795: trailing whitespace.
+**Clem:** One for each of us who watched. So somebody knows we were here.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1805: trailing whitespace.
+**Kera:** Salt-road fever in the coastal villages. The ledger wing sold the cure. We are giving it away.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1806: trailing whitespace.
+**Tilda:** With what staff? You have three shelves and a temper.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1807: trailing whitespace.
+**Kera:** I have you, Iona, and a harbor archer who knows the coast.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1808: trailing whitespace.
+**Odelia:** I did not agree to this.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1809: trailing whitespace.
+**Kera:** You agreed with your face.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1815: trailing whitespace.
+**Tilda:** This is where I learned. My teacher treated this fever with salt and honesty.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1816: trailing whitespace.
+**Odelia:** My brother and I stole bread from that bakery.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1817: trailing whitespace.
+**Iona:** Then we will pay it back with medicine.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1823: trailing whitespace.
+**Ledger Agent:** You are ruining a market, alchemist.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1824: trailing whitespace.
+**Kera:** I am labeling it correctly. Yours says "cure". Mine says "cure, free, and the name of who made it".  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1825: trailing whitespace.
+*The villagers took Kera's bottles. The agent left with a full crate and an empty road.*  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1835: trailing whitespace.
+**Council Herald:** By the seven seals of the Council: any person claiming royal blood shall present themselves at the capital, or be recorded as an impostor.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1836: trailing whitespace.
+**Mirel:** That is new ink. They know a claim is coming.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1837: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** They have never needed to deny a heir before.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1843: trailing whitespace.
+**Sable:** Seven seals. All uncut. The Council agrees on something for once.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1844: trailing whitespace.
+**Mirel:** And this is a court hand I know. The same scribe who wrote the erasure orders I copied.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1845: trailing whitespace.
+**Nara:** Then the hand that removed her name is still in the capital.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1851: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** You read what you are given. So did I. I stopped.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1852: trailing whitespace.
+**Council Herald:** You were a herald of the Crown. You know the penalty.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1853: trailing whitespace.
+**Marek:** I know the price. It is cheaper than reading false paper for the rest of my life.  
narrative/02_Main_Story/PART1_FULL_SCRIPT.md:1854: trailing whitespace.
+*The herald left. The decree stayed nailed to the post, and beneath it someone scratched: WHO GAVE THE ORDER?*  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:7: trailing whitespace.
+**Role:** Female opening antagonist, recurring rival, Chapter 2-5 boss.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:8: trailing whitespace.
+**Age:** 34.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:9: trailing whitespace.
+**Former office:** Royal Inquisitor and keeper of the Sevenfold Crown's sealed records.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:10: trailing whitespace.
+**Motive:** Yseldra witnessed previous Last Bell heirs being used as living anchors. She believes the only certain way to stop the next sacrifice is to remove Fadyme from every road leading to the altar—even if that means imprisoning her. She is correct that the ritual is consuming Fadyme, but wrongly assumes that keeping her away from the machine will halt the curse.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:11: trailing whitespace.
+**Boundary:** She will fight Mahmut and disable armed guards, but refuses to harm civilians or order a public execution. She uses the dead and sealed corridors to delay the party rather than massacre a village.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:32: trailing whitespace.
+**Role:** Male Part I final twist, architect of the Rewrite (the Unwritten Hour and the altar's Hinge, its time-loop design); not a playable roster member.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:33: trailing whitespace.
+**Age:** 41 at the time of the Crownfall; current age uncertain because he has been outside ordinary time.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:34: trailing whitespace.
+**Former office:** Royal chancellor, ritual architect and keeper of the court's handless chronometer. Public history lists him among the dead at the capital's fall.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:35: trailing whitespace.
+**Motive:** Cael loved a kingdom, a household and a future he could not accept losing. He designed the Rewrite around the Unwritten Hour so Veyrhold could be returned to the minute before Crownfall (his public promise; his hidden aim reaches further back, see the 2026-09-29 decisions below). He believes one heir's life is a fair price for restoring thousands of lives, and calls the sacrifice temporary because the hour would be rewritten. His reasoning is coherent; his consent is absent.  
narrative/07_Enemies_Bosses/VILLAIN_BIBLE_PART1.md:36: trailing whitespace.
+**Boundary:** Cael avoids uncontrolled destruction because it damages the historical moment he wants to restore. He manipulates officials, orders and machinery, and treats individual suffering as an accounting error.  
